# Explicit amendment: additional bounded ordinary-field comparison

The original exact ordinary-mechanics control remains unchanged. It passed
for the first one-T case (ordinary-mechanics-r01), but exact comparisons of
the extra two-T and three-T specimens failed (r02/r03). Those are retained
failed exact controls and do not establish bit identity for those specimens.
The first candidate-inactive comparison stopped each gate; the previous
binary has not yet been numerically compared for those specimens.

Observed near-null differences alone do not prove a parallel scheduling
cause. Add a separate supporting comparison, reviewed independently before
its first previous-binary or candidate-repeat response. Run two candidate
inactive repetitions and the previous binary inactive on the exact same
stock-written deck as the owned observed result, with matching actual OMP
thread count and all diagnostic activation variables absent. Retain every
input/executable/FRD identity. Never execute a changed mechanical deck.

Keep all mesh, node/element identities, dataset definitions and nonnumeric
lines exact, apart from the original date/time/compile-time exclusions.
For native DISP values, use the previously frozen component-equivalence
budget 1e-7 mm per component, plus r(v)+r(w) for native FRD reporting.
For the native section STRESS aliases, channels1-3 are force, channels4-6
are moment: use the previously frozen 1e-6 N and 1e-4 Nmm respectively,
plus r(v)+r(w). They are never MPa stresses. Here
r(v)=0.5*10^(floor(log10(abs(v)))-5)+abs(v)*2^(-24), with r(0)=0,
from the E12.5 decimal precision and single-precision reporting conversion.
Record maximum component differences, consumed budgets and exact equality
for each pairing, including the two inactive candidate repetitions.

These fixed budgets predate the original qualifying solve in
bjh-component-control.md; they are reused for this additional control,
not fitted to a previous-binary response. The amendment does not change any
independent statics, member-end, physical support, spring, origin-moment,
owner, case, geometry, load or equilibrium limit. It does not qualify a
building or replace a failed exact control with a claim of bit identity.
